From: fanxiaobinggit <16692712013@163.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: rockchip: set RoboPi2 GPIO0_C2 to maximum drive

GPIO0_C2 drives the dual_battery_c2 output on the RoboPi2 CM5 board.
Select RK3588 drive level 5 for this pin.  GPIO0_C drive levels use the
hardware register encoding rather than an increasing current value; level 5
selects the lowest output impedance (approximately 25 ohms) and therefore the
maximum drive capability for this IO group.

Keep the existing pull-down so the output remains in its safe inactive state
until the gpio-leds consumer takes control.

Signed-off-by: fanxiaobinggit <16692712013@163.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-cm5-robopi2.dts | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-cm5-robopi2.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-cm5-robopi2.dts
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-cm5-robopi2.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/rockchip/rk3588s-orangepi-cm5-robopi2.dts
@@ -1,5 +1,5 @@
 		dual_battery_c2_pin: dual-battery-c2-pin {
 			rockchip,pins =
-				<0 RK_PC2 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_down>;
+				<0 RK_PC2 RK_FUNC_GPIO &pcfg_pull_down_drv_level_5>;
 		};
-- 
